# Module metadata. `name` MUST equal this directory's name or ModuleManager silently skips it
# (ModuleManager::doInit compares the two and only warns when the descriptor is otherwise valid).
# A skipped module here is an install that runs to "finished" having created no account at all.
---
type:       "job"
name:       "accountsetup"
interface:  "python"
script:     "main.py"
# Bigger than managedenroll's 2, smaller than imagedeploy's 60. What happens here is a useradd
# and a chpasswd in the target — fast — plus, in domain mode, one bounded network round trip to a
# domain controller. In managed mode the network work already happened on the page, before the
# disk was touched, and what is left is a directory copy and one offline apply.
weight:     6
